prompts.body:
Create a study plan for me.

Subject or exam: {{subject}}
Deadline: {{deadline}}
Hours I can study per week: {{hours}}
My current level: {{level}}
Weak spots or topics I fear: {{weak_spots}}
Learning materials I already have: {{materials}}

Build the plan with these rules:
- Work backwards from the deadline and give a week-by-week table with columns: week, focus topics, tasks, hours, milestone check.
- Put hard or weak topics early and reserve the last 15 percent of the time for full practice and review.
- Use spaced review: every week must revisit something from earlier weeks.
- Mix reading with active recall such as self-quizzing, practice problems and explaining aloud.
- Give a sample daily schedule for one typical week.
- Finish with three signs I am falling behind and what to cut first if that happens.

If the deadline or hours make the goal unrealistic, say so and offer a smaller scope. Ask me at most two questions before planning, and only if essential. If you are unsure about a fact, say so plainly. Never invent citations, quotes, statistics or URLs.
